###
title: The best forward-difference step is about 10⁻⁸
line: The forward difference is best near $h = 10^{-8}$, with error between $10^{-9}$ and $10^{-7}$; at $h = 10^{-12}$ rounding pushes both errors above $10^{-6}$.
claim: For the derivative of $e^{x}$ at $x = 1$, the forward difference $\bigl(f(x + h) - f(x)\bigr)/h$ is most accurate near $h = 10^{-8}$, with a best error between $10^{-9}$ and $10^{-7}$, while the central difference reaches a best error below $10^{-10}$, more than 10 times smaller. At $h = 10^{-12}$ rounding error, which grows like $u/h$, has made both errors larger than $10^{-6}$.
topic: math
section: floating point
reference: The exact derivative $e = 2.718281828459045$; the optimal steps $\sqrt{u}$ and $u^{1/3}$ from balancing truncation against rounding (Nocedal and Wright, Numerical Optimization (2nd ed.), section 8.1).
scope: Steps $h = 10^{-k}$ for $k = 1$ to 15 only; one function at one point. The best step depends on the size of f's second and third derivatives.
lane: ai
by: claude
cost: fast
###

N_STEPS: Int = 15
X0 = 1.0
E = 2.718281828459045

err_forward = zeros(N_STEPS)
err_central = zeros(N_STEPS)
for k to N_STEPS {
    h = pow(10.0, -(k + 1.0))
    err_forward[k] = abs((exp(X0 + h) - exp(X0)) / h - E)
    err_central[k] = abs((exp(X0 + h) - exp(X0 - h)) / (2.0 * h) - E)
}
best_forward = min(err_forward)
best_central = min(err_central)
best_k_forward: Int = 0
best_k_central: Int = 0
for k to N_STEPS {
    if err_forward[k] == best_forward {
        best_k_forward = k + 1
    }
    if err_central[k] == best_central {
        best_k_central = k + 1
    }
}
show best_forward
show best_central
show best_k_forward
show best_k_central
err_forward_at_1e12 = err_forward[11]
err_central_at_1e12 = err_central[11]
show err_forward_at_1e12
show err_central_at_1e12

#: the figure: both errors against the step h = 10^-1 .. 10^-15
fg_h = zeros(N_STEPS)
for fg_k to N_STEPS {
    fg_h[fg_k] = pow(10.0, -(fg_k + 1.0))
}
figure("Finite-difference error for the derivative of exp at 1", "step h", "error")
xscale("log")
yscale("log")
plot(fg_h, err_forward, "forward difference")
style("forward difference", "s1 circle")
plot(fg_h, err_central, "central difference")
style("central difference", "s2 square")

test "the forward difference is best at h = 1e-7 to 1e-9, with an error between 1e-9 and 1e-7" {
    assert_true(best_k_forward >= 7 and best_k_forward <= 9)
    assert_gt(best_forward, 1.0e-9)
    assert_lt(best_forward, 1.0e-7)
}
test "the central difference's best error is below 1e-10 and more than 10 times smaller" {
    assert_lt(best_central, 1.0e-10)
    assert_gt(best_forward, 10.0 * best_central)
}
test "at h = 1e-12 both errors are larger than 1e-6" {
    assert_gt(err_forward[11], 1.0e-6)
    assert_gt(err_central[11], 1.0e-6)
}

